Practical 3B — Branching + Pull Request
Start from your Git_Practical folder.
1. Check branch
git branch

If it shows master, change to main:
git branch -M main

2. Create feature branch
git checkout -b feature-login

3. Check branch
git branch

You should see:
* feature-login
  main

4. Change hello.py
Make it:
print("Hello Git!")print("Welcome to Git Repository")print("Login Feature Added")print("Feature Branch Example")


5. Add and commit
git add hello.py
git commit -m "Added login feature"

6. Connect GitHub
Create a GitHub repository named Git_Practical.
Then:
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/Git_Practical.git

Check:
git remote -v

7. Push main
git checkout main
git push -u origin main

8. Push feature branch
git checkout feature-login
git push -u origin feature-login

9. Create Pull Request
On GitHub:
Compare & Pull Request
↓
