Practical 3C — Merge Conflict
Now create a conflict between main and a new branch.
1. Check main
git checkout main

2. Create conflict branch
git checkout -b feature-conflict

3. Change hello.py
print("Hello Git!")print("Feature Branch Version")


4. Commit
git add hello.py
git commit -m "Modified hello.py in feature branch"

5. Go back to main
git checkout main

6. Change the same line
print("Hello Git!")print("Main Branch Version")


7. Commit
git add hello.py
git commit -m "Modified hello.py in main branch"

8. Merge feature branch
git merge feature-conflict

You will get:
CONFLICT (content): Merge conflict in hello.py
Automatic merge failed

🔥 This is the merge conflict.
9. Open hello.py
You will see:
print("Hello Git!")<<<<<<< HEADprint("Main Branch Version")=======print("Feature Branch Version")>>>>>>> feature-conflict


10. Resolve it
For the practical, keep both:
print("Hello Git!")print("Main Branch Version")print("Feature Branch Version")


❗ Delete:
<<<<<<< HEAD
=======
>>>>>>> feature-conflict

Save the file.
11. Add resolved file
git add hello.py

12. Complete merge
git commit -m "Resolved merge conflict"

13. Check history
git log --oneline

14. Final check
git status

Expected:
nothing to commit, working tree clean

✅ 3C complete.     practical3c



